hat does Sagar represent?','The sea/ocean.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(877,133,'ENGLISH','General','Who is Badal?','A cloud.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(878,133,'ENGLISH','General','What is Parbat?','A mountain.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(879,133,'ENGLISH','General','What is Jharna?','A waterfall.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(880,133,'ENGLISH','General','Why did Boond feel exhausted?','Because the Sun rose and it became hot.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(881,133,'ENGLISH','General','Which natural force starts the water cycle?','The Sun’s heat.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(882,133,'ENGLISH','General','What process lifts Boond from the ocean to the sky?','Evaporation.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(883,133,'ENGLISH','General','What process forms clouds?','Condensation.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(884,133,'ENGLISH','General','What process brings Boond down as rain?','Precipitation.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(885,133,'ENGLISH','General','What is the movement of water back to the sea called?','Runoff.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(886,133,'ENGLISH','General','How much of Earth is covered with water?','70%.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(887,133,'ENGLISH','General','How much of the world’s water is available for human use?','1%.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(888,133,'ENGLISH','General','What does ‘exhausted’ mean?','Very tired.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(889,133,'ENGLISH','General','What does ‘quite’ mean?','A fair amount.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(890,133,'ENGLISH','General','Name one water body from the word grid.','Lake / River / Sea / Pond / Tank / Well.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(891,133,'ENGLISH','General','Which silent letter is in ‘knife’?','k.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(892,133,'ENGLISH','General','Which silent letters are in ‘write’?','w.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(893,133,'ENGLISH','General','What type of adverb is ‘softly’?','Adverb of Manner.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(894,133,'ENGLISH','General','What type of adverb is ‘now’?','Adverb of Time.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(895,133,'ENGLISH','General','Boond was playing with her friend ______.','Sagar.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(896,133,'ENGLISH','General','Badal is the ______ moving across the sky.','cloud.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(897,133,'ENGLISH','General','Boond went up because it was much ______ there.','cooler.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(898,133,'ENGLISH','General','Parbat represents the ______.','mountain.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(899,133,'ENGLISH','General','Jharna represents the ______.','waterfall.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(900,133,'ENGLISH','General','Boond and Jharna played together for many ______.','days.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(901,133,'ENGLISH','General','Though 70% of Earth is covered with water, only ______ is usable.','1%.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(902,133,'ENGLISH','General','A person can survive about a week without ______.','water.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(903,133,'ENGLISH','General','The opposite of ‘active’ is ______.','idle.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(904,133,'ENGLISH','General','The opposite of ‘happy’ is ______.','unhappy.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(905,133,'ENGLISH','General','The adverb form of ‘quick’ is ______.','quickly.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(906,133,'ENGLISH','General','The adverb form of ‘slow’ is ______.','slowly.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(907,133,'ENGLISH','General','Father looked ______ for the keys.','everywhere.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(908,133,'ENGLISH','General','The baby is sleeping ______.','now.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(909,133,'ENGLISH','General','Rekha placed the books ______.','here.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(910,133,'ENGLISH','General','Boond represents the Sun. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(911,133,'ENGLISH','General','Badal invited Boond to come up because it was cooler there. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(912,133,'ENGLISH','General','Jharna is silent and calm in the story. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(913,133,'ENGLISH','General','Boond eventually returns to Sagar. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(914,133,'ENGLISH','General','Only 10% of water is available for human use. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(915,133,'ENGLISH','General','‘Hard’ does not take –ly when used as an adverb. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(916,133,'ENGLISH','General','‘Fastly’ is the correct adverb form of fast. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(917,133,'ENGLISH','General','Evaporation happens because of the Sun’s heat. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(918,133,'ENGLISH','General','Condensation forms clouds. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(919,133,'ENGLISH','General','Runoff carries water back to oceans. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(920,133,'ENGLISH','General','Parbat represents the ocean. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(921,133,'ENGLISH','General','The story explains the water cycle. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(922,133,'ENGLISH','General','‘Write’ has a silent w. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(923,133,'ENGLISH','General','Adverbs of Place tell us when something happens. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(924,133,'ENGLISH','General','The narrative paragraph should be written in past tense. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 17:17:14'),(925,134,'ENGLISH','General','Who is the narrator of “My Brother’s Wheelchair”?','Durva, the sister.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(926,134,'ENGLISH','General','What does Dhrubo use to move around?','A wheelchair.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(927,134,'ENGLISH','General','What does Dhrubo blow so that people make way?','A horn.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(928,134,'ENGLISH','General','What special mirror is fixed to the wheelchair?','A rear-view mirror.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(929,134,'ENGLISH','General','What word is used to show excitement during the ride?','“Wheeeeeeeeeeee!”','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(930,134,'ENGLISH','General','Where do baba and aai take the children for a hike?','To the hills.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(931,134,'ENGLISH','General','What are painted on the wheels?','Bright colours like blue, yellow and maroon.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(932,134,'ENGLISH','General','What nickname is given to Dhrubo?','The wheelchair champ.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(933,134,'ENGLISH','General','Who helps Durva cross puddles?','Dhrubo.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(934,134,'ENGLISH','General','At what time do they go to the park?','In the evening.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(935,134,'ENGLISH','General','What does ‘baba’ mean?','Father.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(936,134,'ENGLISH','General','What does ‘aai’ mean?','Mother.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(937,134,'ENGLISH','General','What is a ramp?','A slope used instead of stairs.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(938,134,'ENGLISH','General','What does Dhrubo tie to his wheelchair for fun?','Balloons.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(939,134,'ENGLISH','General','What kind of pair are the siblings called?','A ‘crazy pair’.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(940,134,'ENGLISH','General','What season is mentioned when puddles appear?','Rainy season.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(941,134,'ENGLISH','General','What quality does Durva feel about her brother?','Pride.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(942,134,'ENGLISH','General','What kind of wheels are used for hills?','Special wheels with grip.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(943,134,'ENGLISH','General','What type of poem is this?','Narrative poem.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(944,134,'ENGLISH','General','What main idea does the poem promote?','Inclusion and companionship.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(945,134,'ENGLISH','General','Dhrubo rides his ______ through the park.','wheelchair.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(946,134,'ENGLISH','General','The siblings shout ‘Wheeeeeeeeeeee!’ while going ______.','downhill.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(947,134,'ENGLISH','General','Bright ______ are painted on the wheels.','colours.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(948,134,'ENGLISH','General','Dhrubo uses a ______ to make people move aside.','horn.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(949,134,'ENGLISH','General','A ______ helps him see traffic behind.','rear-view mirror.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(950,134,'ENGLISH','General','Baba and aai take them for a ______.','hike.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(951,134,'ENGLISH','General','A ramp is a ______ instead of stairs.','slope.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(952,134,'ENGLISH','General','Friends wait for their ______ to ride.','turn.','2026-02-12 18:32:18'),(953,134,'ENGLISH','General','Durva feels ______ of her brother.','proud.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(954,134,'ENGLISH','General','The siblings play in the park in the ______.','evening.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(955,134,'ENGLISH','General','The wheelchair goes into a shallow ______.','stream.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(956,134,'ENGLISH','General','The poem shows joyful ______ between siblings.','companionship.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(957,134,'ENGLISH','General','Dhrubo’s wheels are painted blue, yellow and ______.','maroon.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(958,134,'ENGLISH','General','The poem highlights social ______.','inclusion.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(959,134,'ENGLISH','General','Durva narrates the story in the ______ person.','first.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(960,134,'ENGLISH','General','Durva is ashamed of her brother. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(961,134,'ENGLISH','General','Dhrubo decorates his wheelchair with balloons. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(962,134,'ENGLISH','General','The wheelchair has a rear-view mirror. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(963,134,'ENGLISH','General','The siblings dislike going to the market together. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(964,134,'ENGLISH','General','A ramp makes movement easier for wheelchair users. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(965,134,'ENGLISH','General','Friends refuse to ride the wheelchair. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(966,134,'ENGLISH','General','The poem promotes empathy and inclusion. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(967,134,'ENGLISH','General','Dhrubo cannot go to the hills. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(968,134,'ENGLISH','General','The poem is told from the father’s perspective. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(969,134,'ENGLISH','General','Bright colours on the wheels show creativity. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(970,134,'ENGLISH','General','The horn is used to scare people. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(971,134,'ENGLISH','General','Durva and Dhrubo are called a ‘crazy pair’. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(972,134,'ENGLISH','General','The poem presents disability as weakness only. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(973,134,'ENGLISH','General','The siblings ride only indoors. (True/False)','False.','2026-02-12 18:32:19'),(974,134,'ENGLISH','General','The story encourages supportive family behaviour. (True/False)','True.','2026-02-12 18:32:19');
