-02-02 19:01:12'),(1170,91,'Approximately how far is the Moon from Earth as stated?','3,48,000 km','38,440 km','3,84,400 km','1,50,00,00,000 km','c','The given distance is 3,84,400 km.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-02 19:01:12'),(1171,91,'Which astronaut first walked on the Moon?','Michael Collins','Edwin Aldrin','Neil Armstrong','Yuri Gagarin','c','Neil Armstrong was the first to step on the Moon.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-02 19:01:12'),(1172,91,'Our solar system belongs to which galaxy?','Orion','Ursa Major','Milky Way','Andromeda','c','The text names Milky Way / Akash Ganga.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-02 19:01:12'),(1173,132,'What is the title of the lesson?','A Visit to Shillong','A Visit to Mawlynnong','Life in Meghalaya','The Clean Village','b','The title printed at the top of Page 1 clearly states “A Visit to Mawlynnong.”',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1174,132,'In which Indian state is Mawlynnong located?','Assam','Meghalaya','Tripura','Nagaland','b','The letter clearly states Mawlynnong is a small village in Meghalaya.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1175,132,'In which year was Mawlynnong declared the cleanest village in Asia?','2001','2003','2004','2008','b','The text specifies that in 2003 it was declared the cleanest village in Asia.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1176,132,'Who wrote the letter describing Mawlynnong?','Seher','Deity','Janvi','Shray','c','The letter ends with “Your loving friend, Janvi.”',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1177,132,'To whom was the letter written?','Mawlynnong','Seher','Deity','Shillong','b','The letter begins with “Dear Seher,”.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1178,132,'Which feature impressed Janvi the most?','City buildings','Beauty and cleanliness','Rainfall','Tourists','b','She clearly states she was impressed by how beautiful and spotlessly clean the village was.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1179,132,'What materials were the huts’ roofs made of according to the description?','Concrete','Metal sheets','Thatched grass','Tiles','c','The text mentions “thatched huts,” meaning roofs made of dried grass.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1180,132,'What was placed outside every house to maintain cleanliness?','Plastic bins','Bamboo baskets','Metal drums','Dust carts','b','The text says bamboo baskets were kept outside every house to be used as bins.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1181,132,'The guest house was raised above the ground on what?','Rocks','Pillars','Stilts','Soil mounds','c','It was described as being on stilts, making it feel like a tree house.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1182,132,'What is a machan as described in the lesson?','A farm','A tree platform','A river bridge','A bamboo basket','b','Words to Know defines machan as a platform erected in a tree.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1183,132,'Who was afraid of heights?','Janvi','Shray','Deity','Mummy','b','The text states Shray is afraid of heights.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1184,132,'From the top of the Sky View tower, what could be seen beyond India?','Nepal','Bhutan','Bangladesh','China','c','It clearly mentions Bangladesh across the border.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1185,132,'What simple meal did the family eat?','Bread and butter','Lentils, rice and potatoes','Fish curry','Noodles','b','The text lists lentils, rice and potatoes as their meal.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1186,132,'What responsibility do children perform before going to school?','Cooking meals','Sweeping and emptying bins','Planting crops','Teaching classes','b','The lesson mentions children sweep the village and empty dustbins.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1187,132,'Who was the 11-year-old girl Janvi befriended?','Seher','Deity Bakordor','Shray','Mom','b','She made friends with 11-year-old Deity Bakordor.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1188,132,'How would Deity react if a visitor littered?','Scold them publicly','Ignore it','Pick up rubbish silently','Report to police','c','Deity said she would quietly pick it up and throw it in the bin.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1189,132,'What happens every Saturday in Mawlynnong?','Holiday','Market day','Assigned social work','Festival','c','The village leader assigns extra social work every Saturday.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1190,132,'Which place in Meghalaya has the highest rainfall record?','Shillong','Mawlynnong','Mawsynram','Cherrapunji','c','The Do You Know section states Mawsynram holds the rainfall record.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:09'),(1191,132,'Which is India&#039;s longest natural cave?','Krem Liat Prah','Living Root Bridge','Shillong Cave','Sky View Tower','a','The Do You Know section identifies Krem Liat Prah.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:24:10'),(1192,132,'Why are Living Root Bridges environmentally sustainable?','They use plastic','They are artificially colored','They grow stronger over time','They pollute water','c','Because they are living roots, they strengthen naturally over time.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:24:10'),(1194,132,'What type of village is Mawlynnong described as?','Industrial village','Small village','Hill station','Coastal town','b','The text clearly describes Mawlynnong as a small village.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1195,132,'The huts in Mawlynnong had gardens full of what?','Vegetables','Rocks','Colourful flowers','Plastic plants','c','The description states gardens full of colourful flowers lined the street.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1196,132,'What material was the guest house mainly made of?','Concrete','Stone','Bamboo','Glass','c','The lesson states the guest house was made of bamboo.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1197,132,'How long was the walk to the Living Root Bridge?','10 minutes','30 minutes','1 hour','2 hours','b','The text specifically mentions a 30-minute walk downhill.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1198,132,'Who stayed below while Dad and Janvi climbed the Sky View tower?','Seher','Shray','Village leader','Deity','b','Shray, who is afraid of heights, stayed below.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1199,132,'What did children do before going to school?','Played games','Cooked meals','Swept the village','Fed animals','c','Children sweep the village and empty dustbins daily.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1200,132,'What record does Mawsynram hold?','Longest bridge','Highest rainfall','Biggest village','Tallest tower','b','The Do You Know section mentions highest rainfall.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1203,132,'Why did the guest house feel like a tree house?','It had many trees inside','It was built underground','It stood raised above the ground','It had swings','c','Being built on stilts made it feel elevated like a tree house.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1204,132,'What makes the Living Root Bridge unique compared to regular bridges?','It is painted green','It is built from living roots','It is made from iron','It floats on water','b','The bridges are formed by twisting and weaving live roots.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1205,132,'Which community is credited with creating the root bridges?','Garo villagers','Khasi villagers','Tourists','Government engineers','b','The passage states Khasi villagers fashioned them over decades.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1206,132,'What could be seen from the top of the Sky View besides Indian rice fields?','Ocean','Nepal','Bangladesh','China','c','Janvi mentions seeing Bangladesh across the border.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1208,132,'Why do bamboo baskets help maintain cleanliness?','They decorate houses','They are used as bins','They store water','They are tourist attractions','b','The baskets are used as waste bins outside each house.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1209,132,'Why did Deity not scold visitors who littered?','She was afraid','She believed in silent responsibility','She disliked tourists','She ignored dirt','b','She chose to quietly clean instead of confronting directly.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1210,132,'What meal suggests simplicity of village life?','Pizza and pasta','Lentils, rice and potatoes','Seafood platter','Cake and pastries','b','The simple vegetarian meal reflects modest living.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1211,132,'Which phrase best shows collective responsibility in Mawlynnong?','Guests clean everything','Children sweep daily','Tourists manage waste','Only elders clean','b','Children and adults clean daily together.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1213,132,'If the villagers stopped daily cleaning, what would most likely change first?','Rainfall levels','Tourism revenue','Village reputation for cleanliness','Root bridge growth','c','The reputation depends on consistent cleanliness efforts.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1214,132,'What long-term effort is implied in weaving root bridges?','Quick construction','Generational patience and planning','Machine-based building','Government funding','b','The bridges are woven over decades, showing long-term planning.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1216,132,'Why is bamboo a suitable material for the Sky View tower?','It is expensive','It is fragile','It is lightweight yet strong','It melts easily','c','Bamboo combines strength and flexibility for tall structures.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1217,132,'What environmental principle is reflected in root bridge construction?','Urban expansion','Industrial growth','Harmony with nature','Artificial engineering','c','Living roots growing naturally reflect harmony with environment.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1220,132,'If bamboo baskets were replaced with plastic, what cultural impact might occur?','More tradition','Loss of eco-friendly practices','Higher rainfall','More root bridges','b','Bamboo reflects eco-friendly village traditions.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1221,132,'Why is Mawlynnong considered socially disciplined?','Strict laws','Police patrol','Community-driven cleanliness','Tourist funding','c','Cleanliness is maintained by collective effort.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1222,132,'What might happen if social work were discontinued?','Improved tourism','Decline in orderliness','More rainfall','More bridges','b','Extra social work sustains organized cleanliness.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1223,132,'What geographical advantage does Sky View provide?','Ocean view','Cross-border visibility','City skyline','Airport access','b','It offers visibility into Bangladesh across the border.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1224,132,'How does the Living Root Bridge symbolize sustainability?','Concrete design','Temporary structure','Self-strengthening living design','Plastic covering','c','Because living roots grow and strengthen naturally.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1225,132,'What moral lesson can students apply from Mawlynnong?','Wait for others to clean','Ignore surroundings','Maintain cleanliness daily','Depend on government','c','The story promotes proactive cleanliness responsibility.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1226,132,'Which feature best supports eco-tourism in Mawlynnong?','Shopping malls','Living Root Bridges and clean streets','Factories','Highways','b','Natural bridges and hygiene attract eco-tourists.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1227,132,'What does the QR code imply about the lesson?','Hidden homework','Encourages digital learning','Game access','Secret message','b','It allows students to learn more digitally about Meghalaya.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1229,132,'Why is the Sacred Groves Forest significant?','It has shopping complexes','It preserves rare species','It is a theme park','It is artificial','b','The text mentions rare species of plants and animals.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1230,132,'What long-term cultural impact does teaching children cleanliness create?','Short vacation memory','Permanent civic consciousness','Temporary rule-following','Fear of punishment','b','Instilling habits early builds lasting civic responsibility.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 16:36:07'),(1231,133,'Boond is described as a ______.','river','raindrop','cloud','mountain','b','The story clearly introduces Boond as a little raindrop.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1232,133,'Who is Sagar in the story?','A mountain','A river','The ocean','A cloud','c','Sagar represents the sea/ocean in the story.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1233,133,'Badal represents which natural element?','Mountain','Cloud','Waterfall','Lake','b','Badal means cloud and is shown moving across the sky.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1234,133,'Parbat refers to a ______.','sea','cloud','mountain','river','c','Parbat means mountain in the story.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1235,133,'Jharna represents a ______.','pond','waterfall','sea','tank','b','Jharna means waterfall.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1236,133,'When the Sun rose higher, Boond felt ______.','excited','exhausted','angry','playful','b','As it became hotter, Boond felt very tired (exhausted).',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1237,133,'What percentage of Earth is covered with water?','50%','60%','70%','80%','c','The ‘Do You Know?’ section states 70% of Earth is covered with water.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1238,133,'Only ______ of the world’s water is available for human use.','10%','5%','2%','1%','d','The text clearly mentions only 1% is available for human use.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1239,133,'‘Exhausted’ means ______.','very happy','very tired','very active','very cold','b','The ‘Words to Know’ section defines exhausted as very tired.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1240,133,'‘Quite’ means ______.','extremely','a fair amount','not at all','rarely','b','The glossary defines quite as a fair amount.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1241,133,'Why did Boond go up to meet Badal?','She disliked Sagar','She felt hot and wanted cooler air','She was bored','She wanted to sleep','b','The rising heat made Boond move to the cooler cloud.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1242,133,'What happens after Boond jumps off Badal?','She returns to Sagar','She meets Parbat and Jharna','She disappears','She freezes','b','After jumping down, she meets Parbat and Jharna.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1243,133,'Why did Jharna make a lot of noise?','She was angry','She was flowing as a waterfall','She was sleeping','She was tired','b','As a waterfall, Jharna naturally makes noise while flowing.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1244,133,'Boond and Jharna travelled over a long distance because they were part of the ______.','rainbow cycle','water cycle','food chain','air cycle','b','The story represents the water cycle journey.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1245,133,'A person can live about a month without ______ but only about a week without water.','clothes','sleep','food','exercise','c','The ‘Do You Know?’ section mentions this survival fact.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1246,133,'In the crossword, the opposite of ‘active’ is ______.','happy','busy','idle','quick','c','The crossword answers show idle as the opposite of active.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1247,133,'Which silent letter is present in the word ‘knife’?','n','k','f','e','b','The ‘k’ in ‘knife’ is silent as shown in Spell Well section.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1248,133,'Adverbs of Manner tell us ______.','where action occurs','when action occurs','how action occurs','who performs action','c','Softly and carefully describe how the action is done.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1249,133,'Adverbs such as ‘now’ and ‘yesterday’ belong to which category?','Place','Time','Manner','Degree','b','They describe when the action takes place.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1250,133,'Adverbs of Place tell us ______.','why action occurs','who performs action','where action occurs','when action occurs','c','Examples such as here and out show place.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1251,133,'Boond’s journey from Sagar to Badal symbolises which process?','Condensation','Evaporation','Precipitation','Infiltration','b','Heat causes evaporation, lifting water from sea to cloud.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1252,133,'Boond jumping from Badal to Parbat represents ______.','evaporation','condensation','precipitation','collection','c','Falling from cloud to mountain represents precipitation.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1253,133,'Travelling back to Sagar from Jharna best represents ______.','runoff and collection','freezing','evaporation','boiling','a','Flowing water returns to the ocean through runoff.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1254,133,'Why is the journey from mountains to ocean described as long?','Because water travels through rivers and streams','Because mountains move slowly','Because clouds disappear','Because oceans dry up','a','Water flows across land, covering long distances before reaching sea.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1255,133,'Which natural system does the entire story represent?','Solar system','Water cycle','Food chain','Carbon cycle','b','Think and Discuss section explicitly mentions water cycle.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1256,133,'If only 1% of water is usable, what does this imply?','Water is unlimited','Water must be conserved','Water is not important','Only rivers matter','b','Limited usable water stresses conservation importance.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1257,133,'Why did Boond feel exhausted when the Sun rose?','She was bored','Heat caused evaporation','She disliked mountains','Clouds pushed her','b','Rising heat initiates evaporation in water cycle.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1258,133,'The word grid on Page 1 includes which combination of water bodies?','lake, well, pond, river, tank, sea','desert, sea, hill, rain','river, snow, wind','cloud, fire, stone','a','The visual grid contains these specific water bodies.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1259,133,'‘Fast’ does not take –ly. Which example shows correct usage?','He runs fastly.','He runs fast.','He runs fasterly.','He runs more fastly.','b','The grammar note clarifies that fast does not take –ly.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1260,133,'Which sentence correctly identifies an adverb of place?','She sang beautifully.','The baby slept peacefully.','Father looked everywhere for the keys.','He runs daily.','c','Everywhere indicates place.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1261,133,'Which silent-letter word contains silent ‘gh’?','write','know','thought','knife','c','The gh in ‘thought’ is silent.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1262,133,'Why did Boond miss Sagar eventually?','Water cycle returns water to ocean','Clouds vanish forever','Mountains disappear','She hated waterfalls','a','The natural process returns water back to sea.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1263,133,'Which stage occurs when Badal forms?','Condensation','Evaporation','Precipitation','Collection','a','Cloud formation occurs due to condensation.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1264,133,'If rainfall stops entirely, which stage of water cycle is affected first?','Evaporation','Condensation','Precipitation','Runoff','c','Rainfall is the precipitation stage.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1265,133,'Why is Jharna called naughty?','It evaporates quickly','It makes noise while flowing','It stops moving','It dries up quickly','b','The text shows Jharna making a lot of noise.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1266,133,'Which element drives the entire water cycle in the story?','Wind','Earth','Sun','Mountains','c','The Sun’s heat initiates evaporation.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1267,133,'Which grammatical rule applies to ‘works hard’?','Add –ly to hard','Hard remains unchanged','Use hardly','Replace with harder','b','Grammar note says hard does not take –ly.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1268,133,'Why is conservation necessary according to the ‘Do You Know?’ facts?','Water is 100% usable','Only 1% is usable by humans','Rain never stops','Clouds are unlimited','b','Limited usable water highlights need for conservation.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1269,133,'Which combination completes the full water cycle depicted?','Evaporation → Condensation → Precipitation → Collection','Rain → Fire → Wind → Snow','Ocean → Desert → Forest','Sun → Moon → Stars','a','The story sequence matches the scientific cycle stages.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1270,133,'Why does the narrative style help explain scientific concepts?','It hides facts','It personalises natural processes for easy understanding','It removes science','It avoids explanation','b','Storytelling makes the water cycle relatable.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 17:11:32'),(1271,134,'Who is the narrator of the poem “My Brother’s Wheelchair”?','A young girl','A young boy','Their teacher','The father','a','The poem is clearly narrated by the sister, Durva.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:09'),(1272,134,'Dhrubo moves around using a ______.','bicycle','wheelchair','stick','scooter','b','The poem repeatedly mentions his wheelchair.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:09'),(1273,134,'What does Dhrubo tie to his wheelchair just for fun?','bells','flowers','balloons','ribbons','c','The poem says he sometimes ties balloons for fun.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:09'),(1274,134,'Which colours are painted on the wheels?','Red and black','Blue, yellow and maroon','Green and pink','Purple and white','b','The poem states the wheels are painted in blues, yellows and maroons.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:09'),(1275,134,'What does he blow so that people make way?','A whistle','A horn','His voice','A bell','b','He uses a horn to alert people.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1276,134,'Where do baba and aai take the children?','To the park','To the beach','To the hills for a hike','To school','c','Page 3 mentions they go to the hills for a hike.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1277,134,'What sound shows excitement in the poem?','Bang!','Oops!','Wheeeeeeeeeeee!','Stop!','c','“Wheeeeeeeeeeee!” expresses enjoyment.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1278,134,'What special feature does his wheelchair have for streets?','A GPS','A rear-view mirror','A loudspeaker','Headlights','b','The poem mentions a rear-view mirror for traffic.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1279,134,'The two children are described as a ______ pair.','serious','crazy','quiet','lonely','b','The poem says they make a ‘crazy pair’.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1280,134,'A ‘ramp’ is best described as a ______.','ladder','flat road','slope instead of stairs','bridge','c','The glossary defines ramp as a slope used instead of stairs.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1281,134,'Dhrubo is called the wheelchair ______.','hero','racer','champ','king','c','He is called the wheelchair champ in the poem.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1282,134,'When do they go to the park to play?','Morning','Afternoon','Evening','Midnight','c','The poem states they go in the evening.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1283,134,'Who helps Durva cross puddles?','Baba','Friend','Dhrubo','Teacher','c','The brother helps her across puddles when it rains.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1284,134,'‘Baba’ means ______.','brother','friend','father','uncle','c','The glossary defines baba as father.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1285,134,'‘Aai’ means ______.','mother','aunt','teacher','sister','a','The glossary defines aai as mother.',NULL,'easy','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1286,134,'Why do people say the siblings make a ‘crazy pair’?','They misbehave','They have fun together','They quarrel','They ignore others','b','They enjoy lively adventures together.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1287,134,'Why is going to the market with Dhrubo described as a treat?','He buys sweets','It feels exciting and enjoyable','It is quiet there','It is short','b','Durva enjoys the shared adventure.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1288,134,'Why does he use special wheels during hikes?','For decoration','For balance and grip','For noise','For speed only','b','Special wheels help on rough terrain.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1289,134,'What quality is shown when Dhrubo helps Durva across puddles?','Strength only','Pride','Care and affection','Anger','c','Helping her shows love and care.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1290,134,'How does decorating the wheelchair reflect Dhrubo’s personality?','He is insecure','He is creative and confident','He is careless','He is serious','b','The bright wheels and balloons show creativity and pride.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1291,134,'Why is the rear-view mirror important?','To admire himself','To see traffic behind','To decorate','To signal friends','b','It ensures safety on roads.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1292,134,'What broader idea is highlighted in the introduction on page 1?','Comparison between people','Uniqueness of every individual','Competition','Uniformity','b','It states that every person is different and special.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1293,134,'Why are ramps necessary according to the poem?','For style','For accessibility','For rain flow','For decoration','b','Ramps make movement possible without stairs.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1294,134,'The tone of the poem can best be described as ______.','fearful','celebratory','angry','critical','b','The poem expresses joy and celebration.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1295,134,'Taking the wheelchair into the shallow stream shows ______.','carelessness','shared playfulness','anger','fear','b','It reflects fun bonding moments.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1296,134,'Calling him ‘champ’ suggests ______.','mockery','weakness','admiration','jealousy','c','It shows respect and pride.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1297,134,'What message is given about friendship?','Avoid difference','Inclusion matters','Ignore disability','Compete always','b','The poem promotes inclusion and support.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1298,134,'Why do friends wait for their turn to ride?','They are afraid','They dislike it','They enjoy it','They mock him','c','Friends also enjoy the wheelchair rides.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1299,134,'The poem mainly focuses on ______.','sports competition','family conflict','joyful companionship','social isolation','c','It highlights joyful companionship.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1300,134,'What does shouting ‘Wheeeeeeeeeeee!’ express?','Anger','Excitement','Fear','Sadness','b','It expresses thrill and happiness.',NULL,'medium','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1301,134,'How does the poem challenge traditional ideas about disability?','By portraying limitation only','By focusing on dependence','By celebrating capability and joy','By ignoring it','c','It presents disability positively and confidently.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1302,134,'What literary device is used by giving lively human energy to the wheelchair rides?','Irony','Personification','Alliteration','Metaphor','b','The wheelchair experiences are described vividly like living action.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1303,134,'Why does the poem avoid presenting Dhrubo as helpless?','To ignore reality','To emphasise strength and independence','To create humour only','To exaggerate','b','The poem portrays empowerment rather than helplessness.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1304,134,'What social reform idea is implied through the word ‘ramp’?','Decoration reform','Architectural inclusion','Traffic reform','Competition rules','b','Ramps symbolise inclusive infrastructure.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1305,134,'How does humour strengthen the poem’s message?','It hides reality','It builds emotional closeness','It criticises society','It creates fear','b','Humour makes the subject relatable and positive.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1306,134,'What does the sister’s pride indicate about family support?','Shame','Embarrassment','Empowerment','Dependency','c','Her pride shows emotional empowerment.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1307,134,'How does the poem redefine the idea of ‘champion’?','Through competition only','Through courage and spirit','Through awards only','Through fame only','b','He is a champion because of spirit, not trophies.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1308,134,'Why is movement shown as freedom rather than limitation?','To ignore reality','To show equality in experience','To exaggerate speed','To mock others','b','The poem focuses on shared experiences.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1309,134,'What inclusive value does the poem promote in schools?','Segregation','Competition','Accessibility and kindness','Silence','c','It encourages support and inclusiveness.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1310,134,'How do the bright wheel colours function symbolically?','As decoration only','As rebellion','As joy and individuality','As warning','c','Colours symbolise confidence and personality.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1311,134,'What is the significance of friends waiting for their turn?','Pity','Fear','Excitement and acceptance','Mockery','c','Friends participate joyfully.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1312,134,'The poem’s central theme can best be described as ______.','Isolation','Empowered companionship','Competition','Loss','b','It celebrates companionship and empowerment.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1313,134,'Why is the market visit described vividly?','To show difficulty','To create action imagery','To criticise society','To show fear','b','It builds lively imagery.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1314,134,'How does the poem promote empathy?','By criticising readers','By sharing everyday experiences','By scolding society','By ignoring issues','b','Shared experiences build empathy.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1315,134,'What emotional tone dominates the ending lines?','Regret','Warning','Optimism','Sadness','c','The closing lines show hopeful inclusion.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1316,134,'Why is the brother described as ‘smart’?','Academic rank','Physical power','Intelligence and awareness','Wealth','c','It refers to intelligence and capability.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1317,134,'What idea about public responsibility is suggested?','Ignore needs','Create inclusive spaces','Remove ramps','Avoid support','b','Society must adapt to include everyone.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1318,134,'How does rhythm enhance the poem’s impact?','It confuses readers','It adds musical flow','It criticises','It complicates meaning','b','The rhythmic structure adds energy.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1319,134,'Why are everyday settings used in the poem?','To show ordinary life','To show fantasy','To show luxury','To show fear','a','It shows inclusion in everyday life.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1320,134,'What educational value does the poem provide?','Competition','Infrastructure awareness and empathy','Fear','Obedience only','b','It teaches empathy and accessibility.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1321,134,'Why does the poem focus on joy rather than struggle?','To hide truth','To show possibility and positivity','To entertain only','To criticise','b','It promotes strength and optimism.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1322,134,'How is equality shown subtly in the poem?','Through comparison','Through shared play','Through awards','Through speeches','b','Both siblings enjoy equal experiences.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1323,134,'What does the wheelchair symbolise beyond mobility?','Limitation','Dependence','Freedom and identity','Status','c','It symbolises independence and personality.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1324,134,'How does descriptive imagery support inclusion?','By ignoring disability','By normalising shared activities','By exaggerating weakness','By isolating','b','Imagery shows normal joyful life.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1325,134,'Why is the poem impactful for young readers?','It criticises children','It models kindness and acceptance','It promotes rivalry','It ignores reality','b','It encourages inclusive behaviour.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1326,134,'What structural element makes the poem lively?','Short rhythmic lines','Long paragraphs','Dialogue format','Technical terms','a','Short lively lines enhance energy.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1327,134,'How does the poem contribute to disability awareness?','By defining rules','By sharing positive representation','By lectures','By strict warning','b','It normalises disability positively.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1328,134,'What is the effect of first-person narration?','Distance','Emotional closeness','Formal tone','Neutrality','b','First-person voice builds connection.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1329,134,'Why is the phrase ‘crazy pair’ affectionate?','It insults them','It reflects deep bond and fun','It criticises','It isolates','b','It expresses playful closeness.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10'),(1330,134,'What larger societal change does the poem indirectly call for?','Isolation','Inclusive public spaces','Less mobility','No infrastructure','b','It supports inclusive environments.',NULL,'hard','english','2026-02-12 18:25:10');
